ason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.7.beta1.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta1 - macOS Tahoe (26.2.0) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M4 (Apple9) - Apple M4 (10 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory - CoreAudio (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen working with the TileSet editor for the TileMapLayer, I noticed that the color of the terrain indicator (in the editor dropdown) did not match what was in the Inspector for the same. Then I was able to make the value for the second TileSet terrain indicator change by putting bits on a different atlas.\n\n<img width=\"1152\" height=\"175\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c8884c03-fa54-4067-b92d-7d2a19e8ed9a\" />\n<img width=\"970\" height=\"270\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aa22ca40-e1cc-40c0-9792-aea2f7d0d6ec\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a TileMapLayer\n2. Create a TileSet for said Layer\n3. Create a terrain set and terrain for autotiling with the TileSet\n4. Use differently colored tiles/atlas from the color chosen for the terrain\n5. Add bits to the TileSet for the given atlas\n6. Note that the color of the terrain in the drop-down has now changed color to whatever color has the most bits selected\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[terrain-indicator-color-changing-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27286358/terrain-indicator-color-changing-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"